oleaut32: round DECIMAL values half to even in VarDecRound

VarDecRound() divides by a power of ten with round_remainder set, and
VARIANT_DI_div() then rounded up whenever the remainder was 5 or more. The
remainder is the integer left over from that division, not one digit, so
any value with a remainder of 5 or more units in the last discarded place
rounded up: 258.40941 to 0 places gave 259. The .NET Framework rounds
System.Decimal through this function, so Math.Round(258.40941m, 0) returned
259 and Convert.ToInt64(258409.41m) returned 258410 under Wine.
The remainder is now compared with half the divisor, and an exact half
rounds to the even neighbour. That is the rule of Microsoft's own
VarDecRound as published with CoreCLR (src/palrt/decarith.cpp): it rounds
up when twice the remainder exceeds the divisor, or equals it and the
quotient is odd. Decimal.Round calls VarDecRound
(src/classlibnative/bcltype/decimal.cpp), and .NET documents
Math.Round(2.5m) as 2.
VarCyFromDec() also rounds through VarDecRound().
Wine-derived change: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/dlls/oleaut32/vartype.c
+++ b/dlls/oleaut32/vartype.c
@@ -5236,7 +5236,17 @@
             underflow = VARIANT_int_addlossy( quotient->bitsnum, &quotientscale,
                 ARRAY_SIZE(quotient->bitsnum), remainderplusquotient, &tempquotientscale, 4);
             if (round_remainder) {
-                if(remainderplusquotient[4] >= 5){
+                /* Round half to even: compare twice the remainder with the divisor.
+                   The remainder is an integer below the divisor, not a single digit. */
+                DWORD twice[4], whole[4] = {0};
+                int cmp = 0, k;
+
+                memcpy(twice, remainderplusquotient + 4, sizeof(twice));
+                VARIANT_int_mulbychar(twice, ARRAY_SIZE(twice), 2);
+                memcpy(whole, divisor->bitsnum, sizeof(divisor->bitsnum));
+                for (k = ARRAY_SIZE(twice) - 1; k >= 0 && !cmp; k--)
+                    cmp = (twice[k] > whole[k]) - (twice[k] < whole[k]);
+                if (cmp > 0 || (cmp == 0 && (quotient->bitsnum[0] & 1))) {
                     unsigned int i;
                     unsigned char remainder = 1;
                     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(quotient->bitsnum) && remainder; i++) {
